From 579cec8c962e75da9e1590739ede0cdd2a5ea101 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:21:50 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: Contrast autofocus with a focus lens

The simple pipeline handler never drove a focus lens, so modules with a
voice coil (the SM-T570's S5K3L6 + DW9808) stayed at a fixed position.

- SwStatsCpu (packed 10-bit Bayer): a focus measure, the squared green
  differences within and between sampled 2x2 blocks over the central
  third of each statistics line, and the green sum it was taken over.
- IPA: an Af algorithm, enabled by an "Af" block in the sensor tuning
  file: coarse scan over the lens range, fine scan around the best
  coarse step, hold; rescan when the measure drops or the brightness
  changes for a few statistics frames.
- IPA interface: setFocusPosition(int32), forwarded by SoftwareIsp to the
  simple pipeline handler, which moves the sensor's CameraLens.
